cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this work, please cite it as below."
title: "SSA Yield Uncertainty: site-specific maize yield response and risk-adjusted fertilizer profitability across Sub-Saharan Africa under joint climate and price uncertainty"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Bisrat
    family-names: Haile
    email: bismignot@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/bsrthyle/ssa-yield-uncertainty"
abstract: >-
  A spatially explicit modeling framework combining agronomic trial data,
  soil and climate layers, and predicted local input and output prices with
  a spatial copula Monte Carlo engine that jointly simulates seasonal
  rainfall and maize price, producing per-pixel profit distributions and
  risk-adjusted optimal fertilizer rates for maize across Sub-Saharan
  Africa under joint climate-price, climate-only, and price-only
  uncertainty.
keywords:
  - fertilizer profitability
  - yield response
  - risk analysis
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - spatial copula
  - Sub-Saharan Africa
  - maize
  - smallholder agriculture
license: MIT
status: in-preparation
date-released: "2026-06-11"
